{
  "schema": 1,
  "about": "Modwerk's Analog Rytm MKII base, built by npm run machine:base -- analog-rytm-mkii: core-ar2 0.7's source unchanged (sdk/imports/core-ar2-source-fb58292.json), with Modwerk's own sources in base/ added on top: in every variant (common) the machine list's sections (mw_machine_sections), the FX track's edit save of words 38 to 41, which stock writes over the delay's TIME (base/fxguard.s), the lean engine (base/perf-*: the audio interrupt's work that cannot change the block is left out, the CPU/OVR mark and the screen rate under a backed-up UI; elekloader/README.md) and pad pressure (base/pad-pressure.s: a held pad's pressure reaches the sound's aftertouch and MIDI during a retrig roll, and CHROMATIC pads send it on the played note), and in send-bus (add) the FX track's lock words, the send bus with its return, its pages and the FX list (mw_fx) send effects contribute to, and digital voices (mw_voices) with the hook ev_sound_applied. A site names the stock bytes it replaces by length and SHA-256; the build fills them from the user's OS. It comes in three variants: send-bus (the default, with add), voices (add without what its leave names: the FX track's lock words, the send bus, its pages, its clock and the FX list, so a set with a digital voice machine and no send effect keeps the voices and pays nothing for a bus it does not use; only the send bus writes those words, so on voices a pattern's send-FX locks are not kept: one saved with them on send-bus plays without them, and stock's next save of all its locks frees their lanes, while word 0 keeps marking those controls locked, so back on send-bus they play the kit's stored words instead, as after a trip through plain) and plain (core-ar2 0.7's source with common alone, for a build with neither, which then pays none of add's cost). npm run machine:base -- analog-rytm-mkii --dev also builds each variant with dev on top: the development link over USB MIDI (base/link.c), for test images only, never a release. Its version is 0.7.1 (version below, in place of the imported recipe's 0.7): from that version on the builder links a set in the 3.7 MiB mod area 0x47B50000-0x47F00000 (the kit's coreDdr, src/engine/elektron/kit-devices.ts), where the send bus's work area ends (sendbus.c's MODS_END); a 0.7 base keeps 0x47BE0000-0x47C00000.",
